# Feature: Auto-Instrumentation

{{ template "chart.deprecationWarning" . }}

The auto-instrumentation feature deploys Grafana Beyla to automatically instrument programs running on this cluster using eBPF.

## Usage

The feature gate is `autoInstrumentation.enabled`. Enabling it deploys Grafana Beyla as its own DaemonSet and configures
the assigned collector to scrape that DaemonSet. `autoInstrumentation.beyla.enabled` only controls the DaemonSet, and
it defaults to `true` when the feature is enabled. Beyla is not embedded in the Alloy collector in this chart.

The Beyla Kubernetes metadata cache is a separate Deployment, `beyla-k8s-cache`. Auto-Instrumentation deploys it by
default (`autoInstrumentation.beyla.k8sCache.replicas: 1`) so the Beyla DaemonSet pods share one cache instead of each
querying the Kubernetes API server. Set `replicas` to `0` to skip the cache. This cache is independent of
`telemetryServices.beyla`, which can deploy a standalone cache and is off by default.

When exactly one collector is defined, the chart assigns it automatically:

```yaml
autoInstrumentation:
  enabled: true

collectors:
  alloy-metrics:
    presets: [clustered, statefulset]
```

When more than one collector is defined, set `collector` explicitly. This is the usual case when Application
Observability is also enabled so Beyla can forward traces:

```yaml
autoInstrumentation:
  enabled: true
  collector: alloy-metrics

applicationObservability:
  enabled: true
  collector: alloy-receiver
  receivers:
    otlp:
      grpc:
        enabled: true

collectors:
  alloy-metrics:
    presets: [clustered, statefulset]
  alloy-receiver:
    presets: [deployment]
```

To collect Beyla metrics without forwarding traces, set `beyla.deliverTracesToApplicationObservability: false`.

See the [upgrade guide](../../UPGRADING.md#feature-collector-assignment) if you are migrating a v3 values file.

## Testing

This chart contains unit tests to verify the generated configuration. The hidden value `testing.enabled` will render
the generated configuration into a ConfigMap object. While this ConfigMap is not used during regular operation, you can
use it to show the outcome of a given values file.

The unit tests use this ConfigMap to create an object with the configuration that can be asserted against. To run the
tests, use `helm test`.

Be sure perform actual integration testing in a live environment in the main [k8s-monitoring](../..) chart.

